- Filters events to the `[Mw 6.4, Mw 7.1]` time window and study region.
- Builds a 1 km × 1 km grid and assigns events to cells.
- Constructs 30-minute per-cell seismicity time series in parallel.
- Computes reproducible grid-cell onset times using the sustained-activation rule from the plan.
- Saves all major intermediate/output tables and QC/analysis figures.
- Emits progress logs and uses parallel processing via `joblib` up to 64 cores.
- Surfaces fatal errors with `traceback.format_exc()` exactly once and exits nonzero.

Main outputs will be written under:
`<PACKAGE_ROOT>/results/exp_run/outputs/01_grid_onset_analysis`

Key saved products include:
- `tables/filtered_events.csv`
- `tables/grid_definition.csv`
- `tables/event_to_cell_assignment.csv`
- `tables/cell_time_series.csv`
- `tables/grid_cell_onset.csv`
- `tables/qc_summary.csv`
- `figures/grid_onset_map.png`
- `figures/study_region_overview.png`
- `figures/example_cell_time_series.png`

